<p><FONT face="verdana, tahoma" size="2" >I'm from LA.  <br>
<br>
Now, that'd probably be enough to say in itself, but I'm also a long-winded bastard, so I'll continue. <img src="images/smilies/smile.gif" border=0><br>
<br>
I've had plenty of riot experience.  The big one, obviously, was the Rodney King riot.  That was the same day that I was moving from one part of town to a seedier part of town.  My friends and I barely got me moved in and got to Jack in the Box before it closed due to the curfew (everywhere else was already closed.  There was almost nobody on the street).  I remember watching TV, and seeing the diagrams showing the violence moving slowly my way.  I remember seeing and smelling the smoke only a half mile or so away.  Thankfully, that's where it stopped.  <br>
<br>
But because I went to UCLA, that was not my only experience with riots.  There would usually be mini-riots after every UCLA/USC football game.  Usually no major property damage, but alot of people running around throwing things.<br>
<br>
One of the bigger ones we had was when Malcolm X came out (I think that was the movie).  The theater in Westwood that was showing it had overbooked, and people got really pissed off.  There was alot of damage throughout Westwood.  I thought about going down and grabbing some free stuff, but didn't want to get shot by the police. hehe <img src="images/smilies/smile.gif" border=0><br>
